## 🧥 5️⃣ Practical Tips for a December Day in Berlin

| What to Bring | Why |
|---------------|-----|
| Warm coat, scarf, gloves | Berlin temps are usually 0‑5 °C; wind off the Spree can feel colder. |
| Waterproof shoes/boots | Expect occasional rain or slush, especially near the train station. |
| Portable power bank | You’ll be using maps, ticket apps, and the taxi app all day. |
| Cash (€) **and** contactless card | Some street‑food stalls (especially near East Side Gallery) prefer cash. |
| Printed/phone copy of the **Reichstag registration email** | Needed for entry to the dome. |
| Small umbrella | Handy for quick rain showers. |

